  "articleBody": "To plan an attached ADU successfully, first define how the space will be used, then verify site conditions, measure the existing home, establish a realistic scope, and assemble the information needed for design and permit review. A coordinated design-build process can connect layout decisions, material selections, permit preparation, construction, and final inspection.",
